# 🧠 Machine Learning / Deep Learning Pipeline

The project follows a standard computer-vision pipeline.

### Step 1 — Image Collection

Skin-lesion images are collected from an appropriate dataset.

### Step 2 — Data Preprocessing

Images are processed before being passed to the model.

Typical preprocessing includes:

* Image resizing
* Pixel normalization
* Label encoding
* Dataset splitting
* Data augmentation where appropriate

### Step 3 — Model Training

A deep-learning image classification model is trained using the processed images.

### Step 4 — Model Evaluation

The trained model can be evaluated using metrics such as:

* Accuracy
* Precision
* Recall
* F1-score
* Confusion Matrix

### Step 5 — Model Serialization

The trained model is saved for use by the Flask application.

### Step 6 — Prediction

The Flask backend receives an uploaded image and passes it through the trained model.

### Step 7 — Explainability

Grad-CAM generates an activation heatmap for the predicted class.

### Step 8 — Result Display

The application displays:

* Predicted lesion type
* Confidence score
* Risk level
* Grad-CAM visualization
* Medical disclaimer

